#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-link.md:1
msgid "llvm-link - LLVM bitcode linker"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-link.md:6
msgid "SYNOPSIS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-link.md:8
msgid "{program}`llvm-link` \\[*options*\\] *filename ...*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-link.md:10
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-link.md:12
msgid ""
"{program}`llvm-link` takes several LLVM bitcode files and links them "
"together into a single LLVM bitcode file. It writes the output file to "
"standard output, unless the {option}`-o` option is used to specify a "
"filename."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-link.md:16
msgid "OPTIONS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-link.md:19
msgid ""
"Enable binary output on terminals. Normally, {program}`llvm-link` will "
"refuse to write raw bitcode output if the output stream is a terminal. With "
"this option, {program}`llvm-link` will write raw bitcode regardless of the "
"output device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-link.md:26
msgid ""
"Specify the output file name. If `filename` is \"`-`\", then {program}`llvm-"
"link` will write its output to standard output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-link.md:31
msgid "Write output in LLVM intermediate language (instead of bitcode)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-link.md:35
msgid ""
"If specified, {program}`llvm-link` prints a human-readable version of the "
"output bitcode file to standard error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-link.md:40
msgid "Print a summary of command line options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-link.md:44
msgid ""
"Verbose mode. Print information about what {program}`llvm-link` is doing. "
"This typically includes a message for each bitcode file linked in and for "
"each library found."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-link.md:50
msgid ""
"Adds the passed-in file to the link and overrides symbols that have already "
"been declared with the definitions in the file that is passed in. This flag "
"can be specified multiple times to have multiple files act as overrides. If "
"a symbol is declared more than twice, the definition from the file declared "
"last takes precedence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-link.md:58
msgid ""
"Specify a function that should be imported from the specified file for "
"linking with ThinLTO. This option can be specified multiple times to import "
"multiple functions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-link.md:64
msgid ""
"Specify the path to a file containing the module summary index with the "
"results of an earlier ThinLTO link. This option is required when `--import` "
"is used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-link.md:70
msgid ""
"Maintains existing linkage for symbols defined in the first input and "
"converts linkage in all other inputs to internal linkage unless they are "
"referenced by `llvm*.used` or are special-cased runtime functions (e.g. "
"stack protector runtime)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-link.md:77
msgid "Disables the use of a uniquing type map for debug info."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-link.md:81
msgid "Link only needed symbols."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-link.md:85
msgid "Disable lazy module loading."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-link.md:89
msgid "Suppress all linker warnings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-link.md:93
msgid "Preserve the use-list order when writing LLVM bitcode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-link.md:97
msgid "Preserve the use-list order when writing LLVM assembly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-link.md:101
msgid ""
"Do not error out when a non-bitcode file is encountered while processing an "
"archive."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-link.md:105
msgid "EXIT STATUS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-link.md:107
msgid ""
"If {program}`llvm-link` succeeds, it will exit with 0. Otherwise, if an "
"error occurs, it will exit with a non-zero value."
msgstr ""
